 — a free KDP account at kdp.amazon.com. Nothing to pay ever upfront; Amazon only takes the print cost when a book sells.
To open it you need:
Email + password (regular Amazon login works, but KDP is a separate dashboard)
Publisher identity — your legal name or a pen name/p imprint (no company needed)
Address (for payouts/verification)
Tax interview — a guided W-8BEN form (you're non-US; the UK–US treaty can reduce/zero the 30% US withholding on US sales; the form walks you through it)
Bank account for payouts — works with a normal UK bank, paid monthly once you pass the payout threshold
What you do not need:
No fees, no minimum, no inventory — printing cost is deducted per sale
No ISBN — KDP issues a free one (or bring your own if you later want Ingram/bookstores)
No exclusivity on the content — only that specific KDP edition file
Then per title you upload: interior PDF + cover PDF (our build already outputs A5 PDFs — just needs the 5.5×8.5 re-trim + a cover), set list price, and it's live on Amazon in ~72h.